>      Monsters learn about _types_ of traps by surviving
> movement onto an instance of the type.  (A few monsters
> such as shopkeepers and quest leaders are created with some
> or all trap types already learned.)  Once a type has been
> learned, all traps of same type are known to that monster,
> regardless of whether the hero has discovered them yet.

<only-nominally-related>

Spork modifies this a bit to discourage monsters from walking into
deathtraps in a conga line.  If a monster sees a particular trap get
triggered, it will then understand what all traps of that kind are, and
will not trigger them again.

This prevents the "everyone falls in pit!" problem in hallways (not that
pits kill things too often, but you get the idea).

